  AssetToken — D5 pause and forced transfer (spec-v1 §5 D5 functions)
    pause / unpause
      √ the issuer pauses and unpauses, emitting OpenZeppelin's Paused and Unpaused (119ms)
      √ rejects pause and unpause from an account without DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE
      √ rejects pause from a compliance-only delegate
      √ lets a delegated DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE holder pause, because authority is the role
      √ rejects pausing twice and unpausing when not paused
      √ does not let one issuer pause another issuer's token (invariant 7)
    pause invariant (restated invariant 5)
      √ blocks transfer and transferFrom while paused and restores them after unpause (40ms)
      √ blocks AssetSale allocate, buyTokens and recoverUnsoldTokens while paused (42ms)
      √ still allows whitelist changes and ETH withdrawal while paused
    forcedTransfer
      √ moves a revoked holder's balance to a whitelisted address with Transfer and ForcedTransfer
      √ works while paused
      √ rejects callers without DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE, including a compliance delegate
      √ rejects taking from a whitelisted holder: a live investor or the sale contract
      √ rejects the zero address as source, so it cannot mint
      √ rejects a recipient that is not whitelisted, including the zero address
      √ rejects an amount above the holder's balance
      √ does not let one issuer force-transfer on another issuer's token (invariant 7)
      √ recovers a lost-key holding: revoke, then force-transfer to a new wallet
    forced-transfer invariant (restated invariant 6)
      √ only succeeds from a non-zero revoked address to a whitelisted one, and never changes totalSupply (331ms)

